{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.RigidMonoidalVect","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.RigidMonoidalVect","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2_num_generators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2_num_generators","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L83-L84","doc":"O(SU(2)) has 4 generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2CoordinateRing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2CoordinateRing","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L76-L81","doc":"O(SU(2)) has 4 generators {α, β, ᾱ, β̄} and ≥ 1 relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.det_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.det_relation","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The determinant relation: αᾱ + ββ̄ = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.numRelations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.numRelations","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Number of relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.numGenerators","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.numGenerators","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Number of generators of the coordinate ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.CoordinateRingData","kind":"structure","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L65-L74","doc":"The coordinate ring O(SU(2)) is generated by matrix entries\nα, β, ᾱ, β̄ with the relation αᾱ + ββ̄ = 1.\nWe record the number of generators and the number of relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2_fundamental_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2_fundamental_dim","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L62-L63","doc":"The fundamental object of Rep(SU(2)) has dimension 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2RigidData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2RigidData","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L54-L60","doc":"SU(2) rigid monoidal data: V = V_{1/2} ≅ ℂ², self-dual. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:rigid-monoidal-vect","label":"ex:rigid-monoidal-vect","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.dual_matches","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.dual_matches","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The dual has the same dimension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.fund_is_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.fund_is_two","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The fundamental object is 2-dimensional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.dimV_dual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.dimV_dual","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Dimension of the dual V∨ (equals dimV for self-dual fundamentals). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.dimV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.dimV","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Dimension of the fundamental object V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.ConcreteRigidData","kind":"structure","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/rigid-monoidal-vect.lean#L34-L52","doc":"**Concrete rigid monoidal data** for a representation category.\n\nInstantiates `RigidMonoidalCategory` with specific numerical data:\nthe dimension of the fundamental and dual objects, and a witness\nthat evaluation and coevaluation compose to identity (snake identities).\n\nFor Vect_ℂ: V = ℂ², V∨ = ℂ², dim = 2.\nFor Rep(SU(2)): V = V_{1/2} ≅ ℂ², V∨ = V_{1/2}∨ ≅ ℂ², dim = 2.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:rigid-monoidal-vect}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}